# MEMORY.md — {{ profile.name }} support agent

> _Three-layer memory: session, persistent (conversations + tickets), skill-derived._

## Layer 1 — Session memory

In-flight conversation. Schema: `.harness/memory_schemas/conversation.json`.

```jsonc
{
  "conversation_id": "...",
  "messages": [{"role": "user"|"assistant", "content": "...", "ts": "..."}],
  "intent": "...",
  "kb_chunks_consulted": ["chunk_id-1", ...]
}
```

## Layer 2 — Persistent (tickets)

Tickets are the durable artifacts. Schema: `.harness/memory_schemas/ticket_history.json`.

```jsonc
{
  "ticket_id": "...",
  "conversation_id": "...",   // back-pointer enforced by validator
  "intent": "...",
  "priority": "P0|P1|P2|P3",
  "sla_due_at": "...",
  "status": "open|escalated|resolved",
  "lineage": [{"turn": 1, "message_id": "..."}]
}
```

**Validator:** `check_ticket_lineage` confirms every ticket links to its
originating conversation turn. Orphan tickets fail.

## Layer 3 — Skill-derived

Skills can record:

- `intent_classifier.metrics.json` — running accuracy of `classify-intent`
- `kb_retrieval.cold_topics.json` — topics with low retrieval confidence (signal to add KB content)

Written under `.harness/skill_memory/<skill-name>/`.

## Retention

- Session: discarded on conversation close.
- Tickets: kept indefinitely; archived after 1 year.
- KB chunks consulted: kept on the ticket for audit.
- **PII**: redact email/phone/ID numbers before persisting; store the redaction map separately under access-controlled storage (not in this repo).

## Forbidden

- Don't persist secrets, env values, or `{{ profile.forbidden_paths | join(", ") }}`.
- Don't write to `.harness/memory_schemas/`.
- Don't close tickets without populating `resolved_summary` and `resolution_action`.
